  "reasoning": "The claim that the Great Wall of China is visible from space with the naked eye—let alone the only man-made structure visible—is a well-documented myth. According to NASA and accounts from astronauts, the Great Wall is virtually impossible to see from low Earth orbit without magnification because it is only a few meters wide and constructed from materials that blend into the surrounding terrain. Conversely, other human-made structures, such as major highways, airport runways, large dams, and cities lit at night, are far more readily visible from orbit.",
